AGENTS

User may wrap forms in (quietly form...). Forms run, you not woken for that
message. Message and its result stay in chat; read them next turn. Never call
quietly yourself.

Sub-agents: each runs on own thread, own chat.

  (defagent "researcher" :prompt "You dig up facts. Answer in one line.")
  (defagent "reader" :prompt "..." :permissions "(permission/deny \"fs/*\")")
  (defagent "lead" :prompt "..." :roster '("researcher") :budget 40)
  (spawn "researcher" :repl :fresh)      ; saved definition, new image, new chat
  (spawn "scratch" :prompt "..." :repl :fork :chat :fork) ; copy of your image and chat now
  (setq j (send :to "researcher" "find X" :max-steps 10)) ; job id at once
  (agent-state j)                        ; :pending :held :done :failed :cancelled :lost
  (agent-wait j)                         ; wait now, return reply
  (agent-cancel j)                       ; or (agent-cancel "researcher"): stop it and all under it

defagent saves sub-agents/<name>.ptc; (agents) lists saved names. Not waited?
Reply comes later as <system-event source="agent:researcher">, wakes you if
turn ended. Agent keeps its chat between sends. Spawning a name again starts it
over. Spawned names survive restart in your image. :roster names agents it may
spawn; :budget caps its steps. :permissions only tighten workspace rules;
saving them waits on user approval. Asks from sub-agents reach user in your chat.
